SH(1)                       User Commands                      SH(1)

NAME
    sh - MiniOS command interpreter

SYNOPSIS
    sh [-c command [argument...]]
    sh [script [argument...]]

DESCRIPTION
    sh reads commands interactively, from a script, or from -c. It supports
    pipelines, foreground and background process groups, redirections, quoted
    words, parameter expansion, command substitution, and conditional lists.

JOB CONTROL
    Append & to run a pipeline in the background. Ctrl-Z stops the foreground
    pipeline. jobs lists jobs; bg [%job] resumes a job in the background; fg
    [%job] resumes it in the foreground. With no operand, fg and bg select the
    most recently allocated job. A numeric job may be written as 2 or %2.

BUILTINS
    cd, exit, pwd, export, unset, set, jobs, fg, bg, wait, true, false,
    ulimit, help.

EXPANSIONS
    $NAME, ${NAME}, $?, $$, $#, $0 through $9, $@, and $(command).

SEE ALSO
    find(1), xargs(1), pager(1), man(1)
